# Dramatic Accusation on Bot1's own Ornithopter (an own creature is a legal "enchant creature" target): the Aura taps it and it does not untap in Bot1's turn-3 untap step
# either ("its controller's untap step", CR 502.3), while the Moxen do. The Aura's controller activates {U}{U}: the creature is shuffled into its owner's library, here Bot1's
# (Bot1's library is shuffled once) and the Aura goes to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Dramatic Accusation
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dramatic Accusation.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Dramatic Accusation.Activate
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot1.Shuffles = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Dramatic Accusation
